# Docker matches these against the full path relative to the build context and
# has no implicit recursion: a bare `node_modules` excludes only the root one.
# Every workspace package has its own node_modules, and apps/web/.next is
# hundreds of megabytes, so the nested forms below are what actually keep the
# context small and keep host build output from overwriting what the image
# installs for linux.

# Dependencies and build output, at any depth
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/.swc

# Python virtualenvs and caches, at any depth
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# Test and tooling output
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/.playwright

# Never bake host secrets into an image
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# VCS and editor noise
.git
.gitignore
.github
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
